Fix: D3D12 buffer <-> texture copies ignore rows_per_image for 3D textures.

wgpu-hal's D3D12 backend sets D3D12_SUBRESOURCE_FOOTPRINT.Height to the copy height. D3D12 steps between the depth
slices of a placed footprint by RowPitch * Height, so when rows_per_image is larger than the copy height every slice
after the first is read from or written to the wrong buffer offset. Height now spans rows_per_image rows of blocks;
the copy box still limits what is copied. 2D array copies are not affected (wgpu-core splits them into one region per
layer). The Vulkan backend is not affected.

Maintained by webgpu-sdk; not reported upstream. Applied to gfx-rs/wgpu at the tag in ../wgpu-git-tag.txt. When it no
longer applies the build fails: rebase it, or delete it once upstream has fixed the defect. The regression check is
tests/wgpu-native/rows_per_image_3d.cpp, run on WARP in CI.

diff --git a/wgpu-hal/src/dx12/command.rs b/wgpu-hal/src/dx12/command.rs
index 99cee37..f4b1bd9 100644
--- a/wgpu-hal/src/dx12/command.rs
+++ b/wgpu-hal/src/dx12/command.rs
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@ impl crate::BufferTextureCopy {
         &self,
         format: wgt::TextureFormat,
     ) -> Direct3D12::D3D12_PLACED_SUBRESOURCE_FOOTPRINT {
-        let (block_width, _) = format.block_dimensions();
+        let (block_width, block_height) = format.block_dimensions();
         Direct3D12::D3D12_PLACED_SUBRESOURCE_FOOTPRINT {
             Offset: self.buffer_layout.offset,
             Footprint: Direct3D12::D3D12_SUBRESOURCE_FOOTPRINT {
@@ -37,7 +37,12 @@ impl crate::BufferTextureCopy {
                 )
                 .unwrap(),
                 Width: self.size.width,
-                Height: self.size.height,
+                // D3D12 steps between depth slices by RowPitch * Height, so Height must span the buffer's
+                // rows per image, not just the copied rows; the copy box still limits what is copied.
+                Height: self
+                    .buffer_layout
+                    .rows_per_image
+                    .map_or(self.size.height, |rows| (rows * block_height).max(self.size.height)),
                 Depth: self.size.depth,
                 RowPitch: {
                     let actual = self.buffer_layout.bytes_per_row.unwrap_or_else(|| {
